%% Figure 4 - Jan-Piet Mens' Ansible host certificate deployment workflow
%% Source of truth: docs/technical-reference.md, Section 10
%% Render: mmdc -i 04-ansible-workflow.mmd -o 04-ansible-workflow.png
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant C as Ansible Controller
    participant AG as SSH Agent<br/>(CA passphrase / KMS)
    participant N as Target Node<br/>(d13)

    note over C,N: Phase 1 - Generate key ON THE NODE
    C ->> N: openssh_keypair (backend opensshbin)
    note over N: Ed25519 private key created locally<br/>private key NEVER leaves the node
    N -->> C: keydata (public_key + filename only)

    note over C: block / always wrapper -<br/>tempdir on controller (/tmp/jpXXXcert)

    note over C,AG: Phase 2 - Sign on controller via agent
    C ->> AG: openssh_cert use_agent: true<br/>principals = [fqdn] + all IPv4
    note over AG: CA private key in agent / KMS,<br/>never written to disk
    AG -->> C: Signed host certificate<br/>(*-cert.pub, type host)

    note over C,N: Phase 3 - Deploy certificate back to node
    C ->> N: copy *-cert.pub to /etc/ssh (mode 0444)
    note over N: notify handler -> sshd -t && restart

    note over C: Phase 4 - Cleanup (always block)
    C ->> C: Remove tempdir even on failure
